\title{Ford-Fulkerson is correct}
\date{2026-11-17T22:28:23Z}
\tag{algorithms}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\taxon{Corollary}
\p{The [Ford-Fulkerson algorithm](00SE) is correct.}

\proof{
We already know [Ford-Fulkerson terminates](00SH), and the \sf{while} loop condition means that it ends when there are no #{s}-#{t} paths in #{G_f}. By [the max flow/min cut theorem](00T3), this means it has found a [max flow](00S2) #{f}—and moreover, that it has also found a [minimum cut](00SQ).}
